! Constructions from the PDF (Chicago 5A, new construction, 90.1-2004): wall U = 0.084 Btu/h-ft2-F (Table 20, steel-frame wall), roof U = 0.063 (Table 19, insulation entirely above deck). The layer resistance is 1/U minus the surface films.
  Material,
    F07 25mm stucco,              !- Name  Not in the documents: EnergyPlus needs the properties of the layer (roughness, conductivity, density, specific heat, absorptances); the values of the prototype, an entry of the ASHRAE Handbook of Fundamentals 2005 library, are used. Only the thickness is from the xlsx.
    Smooth,                       !- Roughness
    0.0254,                       !- Thickness {m}  Source: xlsx Building Summary L9 Exterior walls Construction: 1 in. stucco = 0.02540 m.
    0.72,                         !- Conductivity {W/m-K}
    1856,                         !- Density {kg/m3}
    840,                          !- Specific Heat {J/kg-K}
    0.9,                          !- Thermal Absorptance
    0.7,                          !- Solar Absorptance
    0.7;                          !- Visible Absorptance

  Material,
    G01 16mm gypsum board,        !- Name  Not in the documents: EnergyPlus needs the properties of the layer (roughness, conductivity, density, specific heat, absorptances); the values of the prototype, an entry of the ASHRAE Handbook of Fundamentals 2005 library, are used. Only the thickness is from the xlsx.
    MediumSmooth,                 !- Roughness
    0.0159,                       !- Thickness {m}  Source: xlsx Building Summary L9: 5/8 in. gypsum board = 0.0159 m.
    0.16,                         !- Conductivity {W/m-K}
    800,                          !- Density {kg/m3}
    1090;                         !- Specific Heat {J/kg-K}

  Material:NoMass,
    ExteriorWallLayer,            !- Name  Source: NREL PDF Table 20, p.36: steel-frame wall U = 0.084 Btu/h-ft2-F; R = 1/U - films (0.1496 m2-K/W: interior 0.1197 + exterior 0.0299, 90.1-2004) = 1.9469 m2-K/W. The xlsx layers (F07 25mm stucco 0.0353 + G01 16mm gypsum board 0.0994 + G01 16mm gypsum board 0.0994 m2-K/W) are separate Materials: the insulation layer has R 1.9469 - 0.2340 = 1.7129 m2-K/W, so U of the whole wall is the PDF value.
    MediumRough,                  !- Roughness
    1.7129;                       !- Thermal Resistance {m2-K/W}

  Construction,
    ExteriorWall,                 !- Name
    F07 25mm stucco,              !- Outside Layer
    G01 16mm gypsum board,        !- Layer 2
    ExteriorWallLayer,            !- Layer 3
    G01 16mm gypsum board;        !- Layer 4

  Material:NoMass,
    RoofLayer,                    !- Name  Source: NREL PDF Table 19, p.36: roof U = 0.063 Btu/h-ft2-F; R = 1/U - films (0.1373 m2-K/W: interior 0.1074 + exterior 0.0299, 90.1-2004) = 2.6581 m2-K/W.
    MediumRough,                  !- Roughness
    2.6581;                       !- Thermal Resistance {m2-K/W}

  Construction,
    Roof,                         !- Name
    RoofLayer;                    !- Outside Layer

  Material:NoMass,
    GenericLayer,                 !- Name  Not in the documents: EnergyPlus needs a construction for the interior walls, floors and ceilings; the resistance 0.2 m2-K/W is assumed.
    MediumRough,                  !- Roughness
    0.2;                          !- Thermal Resistance {m2-K/W}, chosen as a round value between the prototype interior constructions (wall 0.159, slab ceiling and floor 0.260 m2-K/W); no thermal mass

  Construction,
    GenericSurface,               !- Name
    GenericLayer;                 !- Outside Layer

  WindowMaterial:SimpleGlazingSystem,
    Glazing,                      !- Name
    3.2366,                       !- U-Factor {W/m2-K}  Source: NREL PDF Table 24, p.38: window overall U = 0.57 Btu/h-ft2-F = 3.2366 W/m2-K.
    0.39;                         !- Solar Heat Gain Coefficient  Source: NREL PDF Table 25, p.39: SHGC = 0.39.

  Construction,
    Window,                       !- Name
    Glazing;                      !- Outside Layer

